    "category": "continuation",
    "source_text": "[row 599] - eres descanchada\n[row 600] - It comes from **“cancha” = court/field** (sports).\n[row 601] So _descanchado_ literally means **“off the field / out of practice / rusty.”**\n[row 602] **It does _not_ mean “off the court physically.”**\n[row 603] It means your “skills are off,” “you’re out of rhythm,” “you’re not sharp right now.”\n[row 604] - How it’s used:\n[row 605] - “Estoy bien descanchado para el fútbol”\n[row 606] → “I’m really rusty at football.”\n[row 607] - “No he tocado el piano en meses, ya ando descanchado.”\n[row 608] → “I haven’t played piano in months, I’m kinda out of practice.”\n[row 609] - “Eres medio descanchado para ligar hoy, ¿eh?”\n[row 610] → “You’re kinda off your flirting game today, huh?” 😏 (joking)"
  },
